.TH BF 1 "2026-11-17" "bf-interpreter 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bf \- Brainfuck interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bf
.I file.bf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bf
reads the Brainfuck program in
.I file.bf
and runs it. Characters other than the eight commands are comments.
The tape starts with one cell and grows to the right when the program needs it.
Cells are bytes and wrap around at 256.
.PP
The commands:
.TP
.B >
move the pointer one cell to the right
.TP
.B <
move the pointer one cell to the left
.TP
.B +
increment the cell
.TP
.B \-
decrement the cell
.TP
.B .
write the cell as a character to standard output
.TP
.B ,
read a character from standard input into the cell
.TP
.B [
jump behind the matching
.B ]
if the cell is zero
.TP
.B ]
jump back to the matching
.B [
if the cell is not zero
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
the program ended
.TP
1
the file could not be read or is empty, or the pointer moved left of the first cell, or memory ran out
.TP
2
wrong number of arguments (usage is printed)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bf /opt/bf-interpreter/share/examples/hello_world.bf
.fi
.SH BUGS
.B char
is unsigned on ARM: a program that tests for end of file (\-1) on input may behave differently from the same program on x86.
.SH AUTHOR
Jaroslav Körner. Project: https://github.com/elPytel/BF_interpreter (MIT).
